{"id": "EUVD-2026-71288", "enisaUuid": "2806ceef-4cf5-3df8-b11f-b4bb5f4b47c9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvxlan: keep the last remote linked during FDB flush\n\nA non-nexthop FDB entry is expected to have at least one remote while it\nremains reachable through the FDB hash table. A filtered bulk flush\nviolates this invariant when every remote matches: It unlinks the last\nremote in vxlan_fdb_dst_destroy() and only afterwards tells vxlan_flush()\nto destroy the parent FDB entry.\n\nAn RCU reader can find the parent during this interval.\nfirst_remote_rcu() then applies list_entry_rcu() to the empty list head,\nproducing an invalid remote pointer that the receive learning path can\nread from and write to.\n\nWhen a matching remote is the sole remaining remote, leave it linked and\nask the caller to destroy the entire FDB entry. vxlan_fdb_destroy() keeps\nthe remote attached while sending the deletion notification and removing\nthe parent from the lookup structures.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:54:48", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:44:30", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2a7c2f00843225d5f037676bca649321f3d024c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a8820c8a7718327e96849782033e7c85a0f6bcfe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8ba68fd6cdd1e3c92b92f25c7e48bf7bd51a183c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4bbc76ee1b21d3bd045d6d819b2bacd30a6372ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d5d4a7b538b52db63927773a8905fcd9f78a42e2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9cfq-2rjh-r5vr", "CVE-2026-80838"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0c1c217f-2ce6-375e-ba8c-4147babce688", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3699266b-a9e1-386f-84d6-f216be28d1ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.108"}, {"id": "4793ad18-e331-30f5-a4e1-fb201898a993", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.13"}, {"id": "7f1752be-94ae-354a-b107-882396b65aae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c499fccb71cb85902b5c5b9ce9c9ae6683e54a8f <8ba68fd6cdd1e3c92b92f25c7e48bf7bd51a183c"}, {"id": "8da207d3-d21e-347e-8f3f-6c6f86857cb1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c499fccb71cb85902b5c5b9ce9c9ae6683e54a8f <2a7c2f00843225d5f037676bca649321f3d024c7"}, {"id": "94b5641e-8b08-3ac4-8ad6-245c8d4d48bd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c499fccb71cb85902b5c5b9ce9c9ae6683e54a8f <d5d4a7b538b52db63927773a8905fcd9f78a42e2"}, {"id": "a2aa9b64-f3fc-34ce-923b-8b6f6df85e84", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c499fccb71cb85902b5c5b9ce9c9ae6683e54a8f <a8820c8a7718327e96849782033e7c85a0f6bcfe"}, {"id": "cd1f1612-4611-3f87-9a22-9be5e8c53f97", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.7"}, {"id": "dfa222dd-6804-314b-bdc2-416eb71d6378", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "eb5ca1cd-0c9d-3d0d-a952-1dfd233959a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.49"}, {"id": "eda2c1b0-7e4c-356a-9863-165a3ec47072", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c499fccb71cb85902b5c5b9ce9c9ae6683e54a8f <4bbc76ee1b21d3bd045d6d819b2bacd30a6372ab"}, {"id": "ee86edc1-f10e-31d2-b333-0184ffd64c48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9d828001-b718-3a89-9a28-f5ecf93b2583", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}